==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_OperationsRespectMatrix  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OperationsRespectMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact lets the model invent an Operation whose (caller.role, kind) pair is outside the permission matrix; the injection forces such a violating operation to exist, so LeastPrivilege must produce a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_015_DecisionStaffOnly
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_DecisionStaffOnly: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AtMostOneEventPerStatusChange  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AtMostOneEventPerStatusChange.als
    rationale: Removing the canonicality fact lets two distinct ApplicationEvent atoms record the same status change for the same application; the injection forces that duplication, which is the structural shape of an append-only violation in a snapshot model.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApplication  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AtMostOneDecisionPerApplication.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact allows two Decision atoms for the same application; the injection demands exactly that, so the concurrency-safety assertion must find a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: ConcurrencySafety, FR_011_NoSecondDecision, FR_012_SingleDecisionUnderConcurrency
      - ConcurrencySafety: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_NoSecondDecision: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_SingleDecisionUnderConcurrency: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CustomerOpsScopedToOwnedApps  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_CustomerOpsScopedToOwnedApps.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact lets a Customer-roled caller's Operation target an application owned by someone else; the injection forces that scenario, which is exactly the FR-013 leak.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, NoInformationLeakage, FR_013_CustomerScopedToOwnApps
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_CustomerScopedToOwnApps: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OnePendingPerCustomer  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OnePendingPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Clearing the partial-unique-index fact lets a single customer hold two Pending Review applications simultaneously; the injection forces that state to exist.
    expected to FAIL: FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer
      - FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_SubmittedEventPerApplication  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_SubmittedEventPerApplication.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact lets an application exist without its corresponding submitted audit event; the injection forces that gap, so AuditCompleteness must counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_016_AuditEveryStatusChange
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditEveryStatusChange: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DecisionEventActorMatchesDecider  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_DecisionEventActorMatchesDecider.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact lets a decision event's actor differ from the actual decider; the injection forces a decision event with an actor that no Decision row attests, which is the precise shape of misattribution.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)

